pgokf THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
=========================

The pgokf extension, its libraries, and its companion tools incorporate the
third-party Rust crates listed below, and the web UI additionally ships two
vendored JavaScript libraries, listed at the end. Each is licensed by its own
copyright holders under the terms reproduced here, and those terms govern that
component.

Nothing in the pgokf AGPL-3.0-only license, or in the pgokf Commercial License
Agreement, alters the terms that apply to these components. Where a component
is licensed under terms carrying source-availability duties, those duties
continue to apply to any distribution of pgokf that includes it.

The Rust section of this file is generated by `cargo about` from the workspace
dependency graph. `pgokf-verifier` authenticates and appends the exact vendored
JavaScript inventory from `vendored-notices.toml`. Committed npm package archives
cryptographically bind each shipped bundle, package identity, integrity digest,
SPDX declaration, and exact license bytes; the authenticated source map and
upstream yarn.lock derive and version the embedded package closure. The verifier
also authenticates the exact cargo-about executable, then runs it twice with
`--frozen --fail` in an isolated Cargo home and cleared environment. Regenerate
the complete file with the checksum-pinned cargo-about binary:

    cargo run --locked -p pgokf-verifier -- \
      notices-render . /path/to/pinned/cargo-about > THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt

